SUMMARY:Family Hand Building
DESCRIPTION:Family Hand Building            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n				\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Sundays April 12 to May 24\, 2026\n2:00 pm – 4:30 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Create together with clay! Families with kids ages 6 – 13 will learn hand-building and glazing techniques to create your own masterpieces inspired by the Gardiner Museum’s collection of pottery from around the world. In this six-week class\, work side by side to express your creativity and develop new artistic skills together. \nEach ticket admits one adult and one child (ages 6 – 13). Children must be accompanied by a paying adult. \nPlease note that your ticket is only valid for the adult and child registered at the time of purchase. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                General : $500\n                             \n                Includes one adult and one child.\n                          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $426\n                             \n                Includes one adult and one child.\n                          \n                        \n               \n                Additional Participant (General) : $250\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                Additional Participant (Gardiner Friends) : $212\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                                Register Now\n              \n                        \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Class dates: April 12\, 19\, 26\, May 3\, 10\, 24\nNo class on May 17 \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information: \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $30 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase kids clay classes at the discounted rate for membership card holders’ children and grandchildren. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n                       \n            \n                \n                    Instructor\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie Fisher\n                    \n                \n                \n                    Natalie is a passionate young artist with more than 15 years of experience teaching art to students of all ages. She is formally trained in drawing\, painting\, photography\, printmaking\, and sculpture. She recently received her Masters in Expressive Arts Therapy from the University of Hong Kong. \n                            \n            \n        \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
