SUMMARY:Summer Camp: Claymates (Ages 6 - 8)
DESCRIPTION:Summer Camp: Claymates (Ages 6 – 8)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Monday July 6 – Friday July 10\, 2026\n9:00 am – 12:o0 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Campers can get creative building their own clay crew of tiny figures\, painted portraits\, abstract forms\, and more in this half-day camp! They’ll explore artworks in the galleries that represent people in realistic and abstract ways\, and create their own clay representations in our pottery studio. \nGuided by an experienced artist-educator\, campers will practice hand building\, sculpting\, decorating\, and glazing figures and tiles made from clay and other craft materials. They’ll also strengthen their observation\, critical thinking\, and communication skills through engaging activities\, all while flexing their imagination in a fun and inclusive environment. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $234\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $275\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    Add to cart\n\n                    \n\n\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    About Summer Camp\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    In our popular summer camps\, kids and teens can embrace their creativity through clay and other art materials in our fully equipped pottery studios. They’ll learn new skills—hand building or wheel throwing\, and various decorating and glazing techniques—in a engaging and supportive environment. Each camp is taught by our experienced artist-educators\, who also guide campers through the galleries to get inspired by the fascinating objects on display. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Camp Schedule \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    8:45 am – 9:00 am: Drop off\n12:00 pm – 12:15 pm: Pick up\nWe are unable to provide extended care.\nCampers will have a 10-minute snack break every day.\n\nDay 1: Introduction to hand building with clay\nDay 2: Gallery exploration and continuing clay projects in the studio\nDay 3: Introduction to glazing\nDay 4: Gallery exploration and using other art materials\nDay 5: Complete projects and artwork showcase for families\n\nWe invite campers’ families for a showcase of their artworks at 11:30 am on the Friday of each session. Please bring packing materials (boxes and newspapers) on the final day to safely carry artworks home.\n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $30 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase kids camps at the discounted rate for membership card holders’ children and grandchildren. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
URL:https://www.gardinermuseum.on.ca/event/summer-camp-2026-claymates-ages-6-8-week-1/
LOCATION:Gardiner Museum\, 111 Queen's Park\, Toronto\, ON\, M5S 2C7\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Kids Camps
