SUMMARY:Summer Camp: Teen Wheel (Ages 13 - 17)
DESCRIPTION:Summer Camp: Teen Wheel (Ages 13 – 17)            \n                                \n    \n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\nEvents\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n	\n\n	\n\n\n			\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Monday July 6 – Friday July 10\, 2026\n1:00 pm – 4:o0 pm \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Get creative on the pottery wheel in this half-day camp! Teens will learn wheel-throwing techniques to create their own functional\, sculptural\, and decorative pottery. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n			\n\n        \n          \n          \n                        \n               \n                Gardiner Friends : $255\n                                        \n                        \n               \n                General : $300\n                                        \n                      \n\n           \n            \n              Gardiner Friends\, log in to access your discount.* \nNot a Gardiner Friend yet? Join now at the Friend level or above to save . \n*Discounts on programs and classes do not apply to ‘Annual Pass’ level. \n            \n                    \n          \n            \n  \n            \n                \n                                    SOLD OUT\n                \n                            \n           \n                \n                \n                    \n                        \n                    \n                \n                \n          \n          \n        \n\n	\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    About Summer Camp\n \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    In our popular summer camps\, kids and teens can embrace their creativity through clay and other art materials in our fully equipped pottery studios. They’ll learn new skills—hand building or wheel throwing\, and various decorating and glazing techniques—in a engaging and supportive environment. Each camp is taught by our experienced artist-educators\, who also guide campers through the galleries to get inspired by the fascinating objects on display. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         \n    \n\n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    Important Information \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n        \n             \n                \n                    \nPlease ensure the course you choose works with your schedule. For any withdrawals\, a non-refundable fee of $30 fee per course will be charged\, regardless of the reason for withdrawal. Withdrawals will not be accepted for any reason within 10 business days prior to the program start date or after the program has begun.\nBy signing up for this class\, participants are committing to abide by the Museum’s Code of Conduct\, Ticketing Policy\, and Studio Policy.\n\nGardiner Friends\, please log in to access your discount and front-of-the-line access. Gardiner Friends may only purchase kids camps at the discounted rate for membership card holders’ children and grandchildren. \n\n                \n                    \n    \n\n\n\n    \n         
